# Trivy Ignore Configuration
# Vulnerabilities reported against Go modules compiled into the cx binary.

# ============================================================================
# BINARY VULNERABILITIES - Risk accepted
# ============================================================================

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design
# Severity: UNKNOWN
# Component: golang.org/x/crypto v0.58.0
# Fixed Version: v0.58.1-0.20261009181718-2f1f834330b2 (removes the openpgp package)
# Reason: The only importer is helm.sh/helm/v3/pkg/provenance (pulled in via
#         Checkmarx/containers-images-extractor). Fixing requires bumping helm to
#         v3.21.4+, which drags k8s.io/* and other transitive updates.
# Impact: CLI never signs or verifies Helm chart provenance; code path is unreachable.
GO-2026-5932

# CVE-2026-78661: golang.org/x/net/html text node coalescing in addText/fosterParent
# Severity: UNKNOWN
# Component: golang.org/x/net v0.60.0
# Fixed Version: v0.62.0
# Reason: x/net/html is only reached via anchore/syft's Java/Maven cataloger when
#         parsing POM metadata; not used by CLI code directly.
CVE-2026-78661

# CVE-2026-97045: golang.org/x/net/html childTextNodesAreLiteral tree walk
# Severity: UNKNOWN
# Component: golang.org/x/net v0.60.0
# Fixed Version: v0.62.0
# Reason: Same code path as CVE-2026-78661 (anchore/syft Maven cataloger only).
CVE-2026-97045

# CVE-2026-33481: Syft improper temporary file cleanup (GHSA-rjcw-vg7j-m9rc)
# Severity: MEDIUM (CVSS 5.3, availability only)
# Component: github.com/anchore/syft v1.21.0
# Fixed Version: v1.42.3 (plus anchore/stereoscope PR 537)
# Reason: syft v1.42.3 pulls go-getter, AWS/GCS SDKs and containerd v2, growing the
#         binary from 86 MB to 119 MB (reverted in AST-188320). Checkmarx/containers-resolver
#         and containers-syft-packages-extractor also pin syft v1.21.0.
# Impact: Only reachable via container image scanning (--container-images / realtime
#         containers). Worst case is leaked temp files on the scanning host when a
#         hostile archive exhausts temp storage; no code execution or data exposure.
# Status: Risk accepted until the Checkmarx container libraries move to syft >= 1.42.3
CVE-2026-33481

# CVE-2026-33997: Moby plugin privilege validation bypass (GHSA-pxq6-2prw-chj9)
# Severity: MEDIUM (CVSS 6.8)
# Component: github.com/docker/docker v28.0.3+incompatible
# Fixed Version: 29.3.1 - does not exist on this module path. Moby 29 moved to
#                github.com/moby/moby/client and github.com/moby/moby/api; the newest
#                github.com/docker/docker release is v28.5.2.
# Reason: Vulnerable code is in the Docker daemon's `docker plugin install` flow. The CLI
#         links only the client SDK and calls ImagePull/ImageInspect/Close; nothing in the
#         binary calls PluginInstall or PluginUpgrade.
# Impact: None. The advisory states there is no impact when plugins are not in use.
# Status: Risk accepted until stereoscope/syft and the Checkmarx container libraries
#         migrate to the github.com/moby/moby/* modules
CVE-2026-33997
